This research focuses on solving the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
\begin{split}
\left\{
\begin{array}{c}
\Delta^2u=\left(\frac{f(u)}{u^\alpha}\right)^{1/(2_\alpha\beta-1)}|u|^{2_\alpha\beta-1}dt, \ \mbox{\hspace{10mm}} \mbox{in} \ \mbox{\hspace{10mm}} \mbox{$\Omega$}, \\
u=\frac{\partial u}{\partial n}|_{\partial \Omega}=0, \ \mbox{\hspace{15mm}} \mbox{on} \ \mbox{\hspace{15mm}} \partial \Omega,
\end{array}
\end{split}
\end{align*} where $\Omega$ is a bounded and has smooth boundaries, and the given conditions on the parameter $\alpha$ and the given function $f$ satisfy certain criteria. It has been shown that if the parameter $\alpha$ is greater than 1, then there exists a standardized solution $u$ for the given equation despite the exponential growth term $\frac{f(u)}{u^\alpha}$. This discovery meets the requirements of the first theorem listed in [4].

